Presidential elections were held in [[Cape Verde]] on 18 February 1996. Only one candidate, incumbent [[António Mascarenhas Monteiro]] of the [[Movement for Democracy (Cape Verde)|Movement for Democracy]], contested the election. He was re-elected with around 92.1% of the vote.<ref>[[Dieter Nohlen]], Michael Krennerich & Bernhard Thibaut (1999) ''Elections in Africa: A data handbook'', p201 {{ISBN|0-19-829645-2}}</ref>

